{{Quote|Search the area for more trespassers. See what else you can find.|Raith, to their squad|audio=Raith1-TheRelicRaiders.flac|<ref name="TRR" />}}
'''Raith''' was a [[human]] [[First Order Raider]] who led a [[Raith's squad|squad]], serving under the [[First Order]] [[Supreme Leader]] [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]]. The [[agent]] led their [[squad]] across [[the galaxy]], searching for [[Dark side artifact|dark side relics]]. Around [[33 ABY]], Raith began pursuing the [[archaeologist]] [[Mika Grey]] as she [[Mika Grey's hunt for relics|collected]] [[Sith artifact]]s to keep them out of the First Order's hands, eventually encountering the [[Treasure hunting|treasure hunter]] on the astronomical object [[Vargos 9]].

The [[34 ABY|following year]], Raith pursued Grey to the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] [[Ashas Ree]] when she went there to obtain an [[Unidentified Sith relic|ancient Sith relic]]. Though Grey managed to acquire the [[Force artifact|relic]] with the assistance of [[Kazuda Xiono]], [[Kel]], and [[Eila]]&mdash;residents of the [[Trantor-class supertanker fuel depot|supertanker fuel depot]] ''[[Colossus]]''&mdash;Raith took two ''Colossus'' [[pilot]]s [[prisoner]], interrogating them for their colleagues' whereabouts. After their squad captured Xiono, Kel, and Eila, Grey brandished the [[Sith]] relic in front of Raith and activated it, throwing it down toward them. Raith and their [[trooper]]s attempted to deactivate the device but ran out of [[time]] and [[Death|died]] when the artifact unleashed waves of destructive energy on them.

==Biography==
===Pursuing Mika Grey===
{{Quote|We've got prisoners at bay. Shutting the droids down now. Situation under control.|Raith, on Ashas Ree|audio=Raith2-TheRelicRaiders.flac|<ref name="TRR" />}}
The [[human]]<ref name="Human" /> Raith operated as a [[First Order Raider]], a group of elite [[First Order]] [[trooper]]s hunting for [[Dark side artifact|dark side relics]]. By the [[time]] of the [[First Order-Resistance War]],<ref name="TRR" /> the [[agent]] served under the [[Commanding officer|command]] of [[Supreme Leader]] [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]]<ref name="Databank-MikaGrey">{{Databank|mika-grey|Mika Grey}}</ref> and was sent throughout [[the galaxy]] to obtain [[Sith artifact|artifacts]]. Around [[33 ABY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> Raith led<ref name="TRR" /> a [[Raith's squad|squad]] of raiders to the astronomical object [[Vargos 9]] to hunt the [[archaeologist]] and [[Treasure hunting|treasure hunter]] [[Mika Grey]], who had been [[Mika Grey's hunt for relics|collecting]] [[Sith]] [[Force artifact|artifacts]] to keep them out of the hands of the First Order. Grey eventually traveled off of Vargos 9, believing she had eluded her pursuers. However, the agent and their forces continued tracking the archaeologist's whereabouts.<ref name="Timelines" />

[[File:FirstOrderRaidersTakingPrisoners-TheRelicRaiders.png|thumb|left|300px|Raith and their squad took Torra Doza and Feyra Fenris prisoner.]]
In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Timelines" /> they and their squad followed her to<ref name="TRR" /> the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]]<ref name="Timelines" /> [[planet]] [[Ashas Ree]] as she hunted for an [[Unidentified Sith relic|ancient Sith relic]], flying three [[Starship|ships]] to the world. Grey managed to acquire it from the world's [[Ashas Ree Temple of the Force|Temple of the Force]] with the [[Mission to Ashas Ree|assistance]] of<ref name="TRR" /> the [[Resistance]]<ref name="Timelines" /> [[spy]] [[Kazuda Xiono]] and the [[Youngling|children]] [[Kel]] and [[Eila]], residents of the [[Trantor-class supertanker fuel depot|supertanker fuel depot]] ''[[Colossus]]''. As Grey and her newfound allies exited the [[Sith temple|temple]], Raith and their [[squad]] arrived on Ashas Ree and ran scans on the Sith temple that showed that someone had been inside the structure. The [[First Order stormtrooper]]s then [[Prisoner|captured]] two of Xiono's colleagues&mdash;the ''Colossus'' [[pilot]]s [[Torra Doza]] and [[Freya Fenris]]&mdash;who had been in the nearby [[Ashas Ree outpost|trading outpost]] looking for supplies.<ref name="TRR" />

===Confrontation and death===
{{Quote|Took you long enough to catch up with me!''"<br />"''Hand over the relic. Now!''"<br />"''Oh! You mean this? I know your precious Supreme Leader won't be pleased when you come back empty-handed.''"<br />"''Now, give it to us, and perhaps we'll spare the children.''"<br />"''You want it? It's yours.|Mika Grey and Raith|audio=Raith3-TheRelicRaiders.flac|<ref name="TRR" />}}
[[File:RaithAshasRee-TheRelicRaiders.png|thumb|right|300px|When Raith's raiders captured Kazuda Xiono, they moved to interrogate him about the Sith temple's relic.]]
After forcing the pilots to their knees, Raith ordered the other troopers to search for more trespassers. They then arranged for Doza and Fenris's [[astromech droid]]s<ref name="TRR" />&mdash;[[R23-X9]] and [[T3-K10]]<ref name="Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref>&mdash;to be shut off and interrogated them about their colleagues' whereabouts. When Fenris and Doza claimed they had traveled to Ashas Ree alone, Raith did not believe them, noting that their group had come to the world with more than two ships. Grey saw the pair in the raider's custody and suggested to her companions that they flee the confrontation in her [[Mika Grey's ship|ship]]. Though Xiono wanted to rescue his colleagues, she explained that the squad was a special variant of stormtrooper she had fled from on Vargos 9.<ref name="TRR" />

However, Raith's troopers destroyed the treasure hunter's vessel moments afterward. While Xiono made plans with Kel and Eila to rescue Fenris and Doza, Grey left the group and climbed to the top of the nearby Sith temple. Two First Order Raiders quickly captured the trio and brought them toward where the other captives were. Raith spotted their approach and ordered their companions to bring Fenris and Doza with them, confronting Xiono about the artifact they had found in the temple. Seeing this, Grey called out to those on the ground from the Temple of the Force's roof and brandished the Sith relic she had acquired. When she taunted them over how long it had taken them to pursue her, they demanded that she hand the object over and threatened to [[Death|kill]] Kel and Eila if she did not comply.<ref name="TRR" />

[[File:FirstOrderRaidersDeath-TheRelicRaiders.jpg|thumb|left|300px|Raith and their troopers attempted to deactivate the Sith relic Mika Grey threw but failed and were killed.]]
In response, Grey activated the relic and threw it toward the troopers and their captives, warning Xiono and his companions to flee into the temple. Initially confused by the archaeologist's actions, Raith realized what she had done and ordered their troopers to neutralize the artifact's effects. Moments afterward,<ref name="TRR" /> the Sith relic unleashed waves of destructive energy,<ref name="TRR EG11">{{SW|url=the-relic-raider-episode-gallery|text="The Relic Raider" Episode Gallery}} {{C|Slide 11}}</ref> killing the First Order Raiders who had attempted to deactivate it. After eliminating the First Order threat, Grey briefly bemoaned the destruction of<ref name="TRR" /> the now useless<ref name="TRR EG11" /> relic, as she had been searching for it for a long time. As she picked up the item's husk, the bodies of Raith and their squad lay nearby, still smoking from the beams of red energy emitted from the relic.<ref name="TRR" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|We were just picking up supplies. No big deal!''"<br />"''Really? Because my scans indicate someone's been inside that temple. What did you find?|Kazuda Xiono and Raith|audio=Raith4-TheRelicRaiders.flac|<ref name="TRR" />}}
[[File:RaithThreateningChildren-TheRelicRaiders.png|thumb|right|300px|Raith was willing to kill children to achieve their goals.]]
The agent was loyal to the First Order and its leader, Kylo Ren.<ref name="TRR" /> Ren likewise valued the skills of them and their squad,<ref name="GOH">''[[Star Wars: Galaxy of Heroes]]''</ref> sending them throughout the [[galaxy]] to carry out specialized retrieval missions. They were willing to use any means necessary to acquire Sith artifacts, including threatening to end the lives of Kel and Eila on Ashas Ree, despite the pair being children. Raith proved persistent in tracking Grey during her hunt for Sith relics, showing no mercy when confronting the archaeologist, and was unamused with her taunting of them.<ref name="TRR" />

==Skills and abilities==
{{Quote|They're not just any stormtrooper. They're First Order raiders. They hunt down relics for their leader.|Mika Grey, warning Kazuda Xiono about the skills of Raith and their squad|audio=Raith5-TheRelicRaiders.flac|<ref name="TRR" />}}
Raith served as a First Order Raider,<ref name="TRR" /> a variant of highly specialized<ref name="TRR EG9">{{SW|url=the-relic-raider-episode-gallery|text="The Relic Raider" Episode Gallery}} {{C|Slide 9}}</ref> stormtrooper skilled in hunting down Sith artifacts.<ref name="Databank-FORaiders">{{Databank|first-order-raiders|First Order Raiders}}</ref> As part of their duties, the agent was aware of how to store the artifacts they hunted safely and how to deactivate them once enabled. Raith led their squad confidently and captured two ''Colossus'' pilots by giving efficient orders and cutting off their enemies' escape routes. They also proved capable of wielding a [[blaster]] and conducting interrogations.<ref name="TRR" />

==Equipment==
While in the First Order's service, Raith donned a [[Color|dark gray]] [[Clothing|undersuit]], gray [[armor]] featuring light gray accents, and a red shoulder [[pauldron]]. The agent also donned a gray<ref name="TRR" /> [[Macro scope|macroscope]] [[magnet]]ically attached to the back of their armor<ref name="Art">{{SW|url=the-relic-raider-concept-art-gallery|text="The Relic Raider" Concept Art Gallery}} {{C|Slide 10}}</ref> and wielded a gray [[F-11D blaster rifle]]. Their squad utilized at least three ships to pursue Grey to Ashas Ree, also bringing a storage container to collect Sith artifacts and explosive [[weapon]]s that they used to destroy Grey's ship.<ref name="TRR" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|I got to do a Star Wars. An absolute pleasure. That session also allowed me to talk at length with @phillamarr Honestly - I think that was the best part.|Tom Taylorson, about portraying ''Raith''|<ref name="TaylorsonTwitter">{{Twitter|taylorson|status/1196494216391577600|[[Tom Taylorson]]|date=2019-11-18|quote=So as Patric pointed out below (thank you!) I got to do a Star Wars. An absolute pleasure. That session also allowed me to talk at length with @phillamarr Honestly - I think that was the best part. 😁 (Waves at Phil in "thank you")|archivedate=20191118182801|archivefile=File:TomTaylorson-PlayingRaith-Twitter.png}}</ref>}}
[[File:TomTaylorson.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Raith was voiced by Tom Taylorson.]]
Raith first appeared in "[[The Relic Raiders]],"<ref name="TRR" /> the seventh episode of the [[Star Wars Resistance Season Two|second season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'', which aired on [[November 17]], [[2019]].<ref name="Disney Press">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref> The agent was first identified by name in the episode's credits.<ref name="TRR" /> Prior to the release of "The Relic Raiders," they were depicted, albeit unidentified, in a season trailer released on [[August 14]] of the same year.<ref name="SeasonTrailer">{{SWYouTube|JkJtdJKCVto|Star Wars Resistance Season 2 - Trailer (Official)|sw_url=video/disneyxd-season-2-trailer-star-wars-resistance}}</ref>

Raith was voiced by the actor [[Tom Taylorson]]<ref name="TRR" /> who later went on to portray the [[Devaronian]] [[Roland Durand]] in the animated television series ''[[Star Wars: The Bad Batch]]''.<ref name="TBB">{{TBB|Infested}}</ref> Taylorson indicated that they enjoyed voicing Raith, having had the opportunity to speak at length with<ref name="TaylorsonTwitter" /> fellow ''[[Star Wars]]'' voice actor<ref name="TFOO">{{Resistance|The First Order Occupation}}</ref> [[Phil LaMarr]] during the recording session.<ref name="TaylorsonTwitter" /> [[Lucasfilm Animation]] artist [[Andre Kirk]] created a concept-art [[:File:FirstOrderRaiders-ConceptArt.jpg|illustration]] of the First Order Raider's equipment,<ref name="Art" /> which Raith was depicted with in "The Relic Raiders,"<ref name="TRR" /> on [[February 21]], [[2018]].<ref name="Art" /> The concept of the raiders,<ref name="BLE Relic Raiders">{{SW|url=news/buckets-list-extra-the-relic-raider-star-wars-resistance|text=Bucket's List Extra: 7 Fun Facts from "The Relic Raider" - ''Star Wars Resistance''}}</ref> including Raith,<ref name="TRR" /> was an original design created specifically for "The Relic Raiders."<ref name="BLE Relic Raiders" />

